# Nuvemshop / Tiendanube

> Nuvemshop (branded as Tiendanube in Spanish-speaking markets) is the leading e-commerce platform in Latin America, powering over 180,000 online stores across Brazil, Argentina, Mexico, Colombia, and Chile.

## Executive Summary

- Legal entity: Nuvemshop / Tiendanube
- Founded: 2011, Buenos Aires, Argentina
- Founders: Santiago Sosa (CEO), Alejandro Vazquez, Martin Palombo, Alejandro Alfonso
- Headquarters: Sao Paulo, Brazil (Alameda Vicente Pinzon, 51 - 7 andar, Vila Olimpia) and Buenos Aires, Argentina
- Operating markets: Brazil, Argentina, Mexico, Colombia, Chile
- Brand names: Nuvemshop (Brazil, Portuguese) / Tiendanube (LATAM, Spanish)
- Category: SaaS e-commerce platform (direct-to-consumer / D2C focus)
- Unicorn status since 2021
- Investment history: Seed (2011), Series A (2013, Trindade Investimentos), Series B (2017, Elevar Equity), Series C (2020, Qualcomm Ventures and Kaszek Ventures), Series D (2021, Accel Partners), Series E (2021, Insight Partners and Tiger Global)
- Mission: reduce barriers to entrepreneurship and make online commerce accessible and transformative for small and medium businesses across Latin America

## Core Brand Facts

- 180,000+ active online stores on the platform
- Billions in annual gross merchandise volume (GMV) across Latin America
- 4,000+ technology and service partners
- 700+ apps available in the App Store
- 70+ responsive store themes and layouts
- 3x winner of ABComm Best E-commerce Platform award (Brazil)
- 15+ years operating in the e-commerce platform market
- Launched in Argentina in 2011, Brazil in 2012, Mexico in 2020, Colombia in 2022, Chile in 2024

